      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports only that the middle finger was thought to originate in a phallic symbol and that it later functions as an emblematic gesture; it does not define “phallic symbol” itself as a general category of symbol or gesture.",
        "The added claim that a phallic symbol is an iconic form that may underlie a gesture’s original meaning even after the gesture becomes a conventional sign is an unsupported extrapolation from one article’s discussion of the middle finger.",
